  "practice": [
    "Say থ three times with a noticeable puff of air: thô, thô, thô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: থ (thô), থা (tha), থি (thi), থী (thi), থু (thu), থূ (thu), থে (the), থৈ (thoi), থো (tho), and থৌ (thou).",
    "Read the common combinations aloud: থ + া = থা as in থাকা, থ + ু = থু as in থুতনি, থ + ে = থে as in থেকে, and থ + ো = থো as in থোকা.",
    "Practice the থাকা family: থাকা, থাকি, থাকো, থাকে, থাকুন, থাকছে, থাকবে, থেকেছি, থাকতে, and থাকলে.",
    "Practice থেকে in its three main senses: from, since, and than. Remember that চেয়ে is often preferred in standard comparisons.",
    "Practice the থামা family: থামা, থামানো, থামো, থামুন, and থেমে.",
    "Contrast ত and থ with your hand near your mouth: ত has less air; থ has a stronger puff.",
    "Find থ inside কথা, কোথায়, ব্যথা, মাথা, প্রথম, পৃথিবী, পথ, সাথে, অর্থ, and যথেষ্ট.",
    "Recognize these phrases instantly: তুমি কোথায় থাকো, আমি এখানে থাকি, কোথা থেকে, থামো, and গাড়ি থামাও."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "থ is a common Bangla consonant pronounced as an aspirated dental t with a noticeable puff of air.",
    "It is not normally the English th sound in think or this. Think of ত as t and থ as the same type of consonant with extra air.",
    "There are fewer everyday words beginning with থ than with ক, প, স, or ম, but থাকা, থেকে, and থামা are exceptionally useful.",
    "থাকা can mean to stay, live, remain, or be located, depending on context.",
    "থেকে can mean from, since, or than. In standard or formal comparisons, চেয়ে is often preferred.",
    "Best থ words to memorize include থাকা, থাকি, থাকো, থাকে, থাকবে, থেকে, থামা, থামো, থামানো, থালা, থানা, and থুতনি, plus common words containing থ such as কথা, কোথায়, মাথা, ব্যথা, প্রথম, পথ, পৃথিবী, and যথেষ্ট."
  ]
